WOW-BG3 benilla patch 0092: small doodads between the camera and her phase out, whole; so do the units on a storey going away.

The design rule for what stands between the camera and the character: ceilings, bushes, skinny trees
and posts phase out; walls get the see-through opening (0090); mountains, rocks and big trees the
camera bumps into (the plugin's eye clearance). 0091 took the ceilings. This is the doodads.

BG3 marks each object by hand on its root templates (`Fadeable`: the whole piece fades; `SeeThrough`:
the capsule cut; `CollideWithCamera`, nearly unused). WoW has no such flag, so the line is drawn on
WoW's collision hulls: a placement measuring under 4 yd on the smallest side of its own box (the
model's axes times its scale, so turning a piece changes nothing) is BG3's `Fadeable`, and fades; one at 4 yd or more is what the camera bumps into; a WMO's own surfaces
are BG3's `SeeThrough`. The plugin reads the same hulls through the server's vmaps (`wow_arena.py`
tags a big M2 kind 5), so a piece does one or the other.

- `phase_out.rs` (new): the line, the sight lines (eye to her feet, chest, head), the fade clock at
  BG3's `FadeOutSpeed` 5.0, and the entity-path doodads (animated, billboarded, blended), whose level
  rides in bits 14..=18 of the exterior `MeshTag` payload. An interior prop's tag holds its probe slot
  there, a slot props with the same light share, so its level goes through the rig field instead: the
  top sixteen rig slots are never allocated and each stands for one level.
- static_gx: each cell and prop region keeps its small placements as of the last bake (box and items,
  `GxPiece`); `cull.rs` walks their fades and publishes per-item levels; `render.rs` writes them into
  the record's fade bits 0091 added, the larger of the storey's and the piece's winning.
- `static_gx.wgsl`: a small placement's item (record bit 20) takes no see-through cut; it fades whole. A
  big doodad keeps the cut: WoW's collision has a big tree's trunk and not its canopy, so the camera
  bumps the trunk and ends up under leaves (BG3 marks 163 of its 345 trees `SeeThrough`).
- Units: 0091 hid a unit on a storey going away at once, so it popped while the floor under it
  dissolved. It now fades with the storey by rig slot (`UnitFades`, a region after 0090's noise,
  read by `wow_model.wgsl` whichever payload the tag holds), its gear on rider slots with it, and is
  hidden only once gone.
